-- title:
--   Independence of the whole shifted Lévy future process from the full past filtration from finite-cylinder independence
-- statement:
--   For a canonical spectrally negative Lévy process X, a deterministic time s, and the FULL filtration F_s, suppose that for EVERY finite set I of future nonnegative times, the joint sigma algebra generated by all coordinates X_(s+t)-X_s with t in I is independent of F_s. Then the sigma algebra of the WHOLE future shifted process indexed by every nonnegative real time is independent of F_s. The proof is a genuine infinite-dimensional finite-cylinder closure: finite cylinder sigma algebras are monotone under inclusion of finite time sets, contained in the ambient measurable space by adaptedness, and their supremum equals the sigma algebra of the full function-valued shifted process using pinned Mathlib MeasurableSpace.comap_process_pi. Pinned indep_iSup_of_monotone yields the desired independence. This direct full-filtration result is stronger for conditional Markov applications than just independence from an arbitrary measurable past statistic and avoids invoking càdlàg path reconstruction for sigma independence. Uniform joint finite-cylinder independence remains a required, nontrivial hypothesis, to be derived separately from the original independent-increments axiom.
-- source:
--   Pinned Mathlib MeasurableSpace.comap_process_pi, ProbabilityTheory.indep_iSup_of_monotone in Mathlib.Probability.Independence.Basic, original Levy adaptedness and IsProbabilityMeasure. Contrasts accepted countable path bridge UUID 42f8ec77-38ce-4b1d-a188-33f6193cea0e and published full-process/H bridge UUID 7b8aa9ab-9dc6-4b9a-a595-32d384e805ca.

